  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trauma Programme- HHC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main work of HHC-Rwanda is to help orphans. It intervenes on aspects that touch the day to day life of a household such as health, education, food security, justice, habitat, etc. In 2008, within the psychosocial programme, it planned to build a new third Day Centre; the two already built started receiving children aged between 3 and 5 years. HHC planned to build capacity of its APS and Community volunteers: 40 new APS to be trained and 30 community volunteers refreshed in various topics related to trauma and accompaniment of orphans head of households. Personnel development workshops are planned for 25 people and stepping stones training will be held for communities. Trauma healing activities: counselling, clinical supervision will continue.</narrative>
  </description>
